  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen2.5-coder-0.5b-real-tensor-v9.json records one real Qwen tensor FPQ transform/reconstruction, not a model execution receipt
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-bitnetcpp-arm-build-refusal.json records that the unmodified official BitNet.cpp ARM build did not reach model execution on the stated host
  witness cmd/BonfyreFPQ/results/2026-09-11-bitnetcpp-official-model-patched-diagnostic.json records Microsoft BitNet-b1.58-2B-4T (332 tensors; 210 I2_S) through an actual patched-diagnostic BitNet.cpp ARM execution. It proves only model execution; the completion failed its exact instruction after the loader warned of degraded generation quality, so no embedding/reranking or production inference claim follows
  witness cmd/BonfyreQwenFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen-native-fp16-execution.json records 24-layer native execution and four generated tokens from the existing Qwen FPQ0 artifact, while naming that all 290 tensors stayed passthrough and no compressed FPQ execution occurred
