  known_gap native FPQ0 now has a native-Qwen execution baseline but still lacks a per-tensor/block representation passport, non-passthrough block-local decode, prepared residency and parity envelope. BitNet.cpp now has a patched-diagnostic ARM model execution receipt, while the unmodified upstream build remains refused and the observed degraded completion disqualifies it from embedding/reranking or ResourceAdmission until a compatible model/tokenizer path has a measured preservation envelope

architecture model-representation-passport-registry
  canonical_name ModelRepresentationPassportRegistry
  family model
  domain Model / Representation Admission
  layer model/representation
  semantic_question Which measured model representation may be forwarded for which operation, and what exact preservation gate remains before resource admission?
  purpose ModelCatalog stores one normalized representation passport per physical/runtime form with a receipt digest, operation scope, quality envelope and ADMIT/DEFER/REJECT state. It forwards typed compute advertisements through AddressPlane but never turns a model declaration, transform receipt or physical fit into runnable inference.
  maturity implemented
  owns ModelRepresentationPassport
  consumes ModelPassport
  publishes CandidateAdvertisement
  node_types ModelRepresentationPassport
  edge_types represented_as
  edge_types measured_by
  edge_types admitted_for
  invariant a bare ModelCatalog row advertises operation catalog only; generation, embedding and rerank coordinates require a separate representation passport
  invariant only a measured passport whose exact ModelCatalog gate returns ADMIT can proceed to ResourceAdmission
  invariant a provider embedding passport names its source and ordered physical-vector digests, while a rank receipt may carry only a query digest and candidate handles; neither representation becomes the caller's semantic owner
  forbidden_inference a representation receipt -> model identity, semantic quality, provider readiness, authorization, evidence, or effect
  forbidden_inference ResourceAdmission physical fit -> representation preservation or model execution eligibility
  source_path cmd/BonfyreModel/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreQwenFPQ/results/2026-09-11-qwen-native-fp16-representation-passport.json
  witness cmd/BonfyreModel/tests/representation_passport_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreExternalEstate/tests/model_representation_owner_test.sh
  witness estate/generated/mistral-publication-embedding-witness-2026-09.json
  witness estate/generated/mistral-publication-retrieval-evaluation-2026-09.json
  interacts model-representation-passport-forwards-address-candidate
  source_lineage native model catalog and FPQ/Qwen receipt estate
  known_gap the recorded native-Qwen baseline is intentionally DEFER because it is all native-F16 passthrough with no task/production or compressed-FPQ parity envelope. BitNet's patched diagnostic execution remains outside this registry because the exact model-body passport and compatible tokenizer/ranking preservation envelope are still absent.
  invariant representation-record reads the passport's receipt_ref now and refuses a passport whose receipt is unreadable or whose sha256 differs from receipt_digest; a passport is never recorded on trust
  invariant the catalogue sync projects every registry passport as a representation node (category = admission state, source_hash = receipt digest, json_data = the full typed passport) joined to its model by has_representation/represents_model; the served catalogue and the registry hold the same passports
  invariant a failed passport node or edge write aborts the catalogue refresh and rolls the previous projection back rather than committing a partial passport graph
  forbidden_inference a projected passport node -> admission; DEFER travels with it and Model Commons shows it as DEFER
  forbidden_inference a static embedding's neighbour overlap with its teacher -> retrieval quality, or the teacher's own quality
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_catalog.c
  source_path estate/generated/nomic-static-128-representation-passport-2026-10.json
  source_path estate/generated/nomic-embed-text-onnx-representation-passport-2026-10.json
  witness 2026-10-30 live registry and served catalogue agree exactly: 23 models and 4 passports in models.db, 23 model nodes and 4 representation nodes in catalog.db, no registry row or passport missing from the catalogue (attach-and-diff query); all four receipt digests re-read and match
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/catalog_model_sync_test.c exercises bootstrap recipe model rebuild, unknown model provenance, unavailable and malformed registries, absent and malformed passport tables, write rollback, and removal from a valid empty registry
  invariant a model registry refresh fails and rolls back if its prior projection cannot be read or if prior passports exist without a readable passport table; a registry without passports can bootstrap before any passport is projected
  witness cmd/BonfyreModel/tests/representation_passport_test.sh deletes passport edges in an isolated catalogue, verifies a shared-library resync restores both directions, and injects an edge-write failure to verify rollback
  witness estate/generated/nomic-static-128-teacher-agreement-site-passages-2026-10-30.json
  witness estate/generated/nomic-static-128-teacher-agreement-publication-titles-2026-10-30.json
  known_gap nomic-static-128 and nomic-embed-text-onnx now carry measured DEFER passports: teacher agreement (18.5 percent top-10 overlap on 1703 site passages, 20.7 percent on 2000 publication titles) and teacher residency (peak 280 MB against a 275 MB grant). Neither has a relevance judgement, false-prune trial or ComparabilityContract, so no passport here is ADMIT and no cross-model quality comparison is supported
  known_gap eight other organs resync the catalogue through libbonfyre (Capability, Family, Layer, QwenFPQ, Runtime, Recipe, Run, Workflow). Their installed copies predate the passport projection: a resync by one of them keeps representation nodes but drops their model edges (delete of the model: scope) until bonfyre-model next resyncs or those organs are relinked
  known_gap Mistral Embed now has one complete 22,962-body physical embedding representation and a narrow four-query top-3 retrieval witness, but its full passport remains DEFER until a declared preservation envelope and false-prune trial are measured; it cannot be compared with Nomic or BitNet without a ComparabilityContract.

