architecture model-commons
  canonical_name ModelCommons
  family model
  domain Model / The model estate as a page
  layer presentation
  semantic_question What models does this estate hold, which exact local native candidate can this account review, and what output and metered usage did that one admitted run produce?
  purpose Model catalogue pages retain their measured relations and unresolved references. A separate native execution surface lists the current MoE owner's chat candidates and admits one bounded account-owned request through Fabric after explicit review. Model detail joins only an exact native-owned catalogue binding. Served at /s/models/all and /s/model/<id>.
  maturity measured
  node_types CatalogueModel
  node_types CatalogueRelation
  node_types AccountModelReview
  node_types ModelPhysicalAttempt
  consumes CatalogueModel
  consumes NativeModelCandidate
  publishes AccountScopedModelRequest
  native_format MessagePack browser activity carrier, private review intents and retained native execution receipts
  native_format existing llama-compatible JSON protocol is confined to the current MoE adapter; it is not the Aurekai or Fabric account transport
  edge_types powers
  edge_types derived_from
  internal_calculus the catalogue held all of this and had no page. bonfyre-model list prints names and sizes, and everything that makes a model legible -- its variants, what it came from, what depends on it -- was reachable only by querying the graph by hand
  internal_calculus a relation is a dependency only if the thing at the other end exists. Counting an edge whose target was never registered is how one model came to look as though seven recipes depended on it while its own page could name one
  internal_calculus an unresolved reference is information, not noise: a recipe that uses a model is a real relation even when the recipe was never inserted, so it is named as unfollowable rather than dropped by the join that could not follow it
  internal_calculus a model with a measured representation passport is not unmeasured: the page printed "nothing has been measured" beside a registry that held a measured passport, because the catalogue never carried passports. The passport is shown with its admission state and envelope, never turned into a score
  internal_calculus a measured figure is printed only where one exists. A zero for mean F1 is an absence of measurement, and printing it as a score would make a model that has never been evaluated look like one that failed
  internal_calculus catalogue prices remain observations; a reviewed run separately reads the native Meter rate effective at its attempt time. Measured output bytes and duration produce a physical usage event; absent rates remain unknown and do not become free usage
  invariant every relation figure counts only edges whose other end resolves to a registered node
  invariant unresolved references are counted in their own right and named on the model that carries them
  invariant reading a catalogue or native capability list never pulls a model, acquires a lease or starts inference
  invariant account write authority is resolved at the native page boundary and rechecked by Auth and CMS before the local lease and physical model dispatch; a browser expectedBinding must still name the exact actor and destination
  invariant one retained review binds the prompt digest, native candidate witness, maximum tokens, timeout, one-call budget and observed unit rate; a new submission identity cannot reuse that delegation for another task
  invariant the exact native lease must name the reviewed checkpoint and a live residency memory grant before the prompt is sent; fallback substitution and changed residency are refused or retained as uncertain
  invariant a retained physical attempt cannot be replayed after restart, timeout, cancellation or a lost acknowledgement. Meter reconciliation can only repeat the exact retained usage payload for a completed output
  invariant outputs and recipient notifications derive from trusted task scope in the existing Fabric store; historical operator work is never adopted into a customer account
  forbidden_inference a registered model -> a cached, licensed, or runnable one
  forbidden_inference a recorded edge -> a guarantee about either end of it, or a licence that travels along it
  forbidden_inference powering a capability -> authority to invoke it, or a claim this is the only model that could
  forbidden_inference an absent price -> a free model; it means no provider has published a rate this estate admitted, and the electricity and time are unmeasured
  forbidden_inference a derivation -> a licence inherited from what it was derived from
  forbidden_inference an exact catalogue binding or a native memory grant -> a representation passport, model licence or measured semantic quality
  forbidden_inference a native response timeout or client cancellation -> proof the model performed no work
  forbidden_inference a model output -> authority, executable instructions or a confirmed external effect
  forbidden_inference local MoE execution -> distributed peer inference or hosted-provider spending authority
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/model_catalogue_index.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/glyph_set.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_commons_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_catalogue_index_test.c checks catalogue card icons, escaped content and separately disclosed unresolved references
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_catalogue_index_test.c checks public model pages describe local file sources without disclosing their machine paths while retaining external source coordinates
  invariant a public model page describes local file sources without exposing the local filesystem path; the catalogue retains the original source record
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_commons_test.sh checks escaped price observation dates and a focusable scroll region for the hosted price table
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/activity_workspace.h
  source_path integrations/browser/aurekai-model.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/fabric_model.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/native_model.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/native_meter.mjs
  source_path integrations/estate/llama_generation.mjs
  witness 2026-09-26 served from the live catalogue: 22 models, 201 layer artifacts, 134 capabilities, and the relations split honestly into 177 that resolve and 547 that do not
  witness 2026-09-26 the 547 unresolved edges are a real defect in the catalogue, not a rendering choice: they name recipe and layer ids that were never inserted as nodes. Llama 3 8B Instruct carries eight uses_model edges of which one resolves, and its page now names all seven recipes it references and cannot follow
  witness 2026-09-26 the first version of the index counted those edges, reporting nine dependents for a model whose own page could name two. The figures are now joined through the node table and the unresolved count is shown beside them
  witness 2026-09-26 held by cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_commons_test.sh, whose fixture gives one model a real dependent plus two phantom recipes and a phantom layer, and asserts the dependent count excludes all three, the unresolved count includes all three, each is named on the model's page, a clean model is not flagged, a measured figure shows only where one exists, and an unregistered model is refused
  witness 2026-10-30 cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/model_commons_test.sh gives a model a measured DEFER passport node and asserts the page shows the passport, its state, envelope and receipt, does not call that model unmeasured, and gives no passport to a model without one; run against a scratch build, and against a copy of the live catalogue where /s/model/nomic-static-128 showed "measured embedding, DEFER"
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_model.test.mjs checks durable account-bound review, exact submission recovery after expiry and restart, one-call consumption, fresh authority and rate refusal, scoped output integrity, cancellation uncertainty and usage-only reconciliation
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/native_model.test.mjs checks the current native MoE protocol, exact lease and residency, bounded response bytes, cancellation propagation and explicit native-owned catalogue mapping
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_model_pipeline.test.mjs traverses the real Fabric queue and store, a controlled loopback MoE wire witness, compiled BonfyreMeter, recipient activity and the browser decoder; this is not a live model inference claim
  known_gap little has been measured about these models here: four representation passports for four models, all DEFER (mistral-embed coverage, bitnet diagnostic, nomic-embed-text-onnx residency, nomic-static-128 teacher agreement). A model page shows each passport with its state and envelope; the other nineteen models still say nothing has been measured, and no quality comparison across models is supported
  known_gap catalogue entries without an explicit BONFYRE_MODEL_BINDINGS_FILE mapping remain catalogue-only. The model index separately lists actual configured native candidates without inferring a catalogue match
  known_gap verification uses a controlled MoE protocol witness and the real native meter in isolated stores; it does not establish the live model's availability, performance, licence or production quality, and does not resume an operator STOP
  known_gap the passport band is in checkout source and held by the test, but the running releases predate it: the live page will not show passports until a WebAddress release carries it
  known_gap hosted token usage in BonfyreMeter (codex and claude models) names no model this catalogue registers, so there is no exact meter-to-catalogue join; none is inferred
  known_gap the 547 unresolved references are reported and not repaired. Whether those recipes and layers should be registered nodes or should stop being referenced is a question about the catalogue, not about this page
  interacts model-commons-reads-the-catalogue
  interacts model-commons-admits-native-account-work
  interacts model-commons-records-physical-usage
  interacts account-work-names-provider-sessions-for-meter

interaction model-commons-reads-the-catalogue
  source model-commons
  destination model-topology-graph
  relation reads_without_asserting
  preserves the catalogue as the owner of what is registered: these pages read it and write nothing
  drops any path by which rendering a model could register, pull, cache or run one
  forbidden_inference a rendered model page -> a model this estate has ever executed
  witness 2026-09-26 both rooms open the catalogue read-only and no request pulls, verifies or caches anything
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c

interaction model-commons-admits-native-account-work
  source model-commons
  destination dual-agent-fabric-native-owner
  relation reviewed-account-delegation
  preserves fresh native actor and destination admission, one physical request, original task identity, native lease, STOP, queue budgets, output ownership and recipient notifications
  drops browser-selected paths, hosts, process arguments, retroactive operator task attribution and automatic retries of uncertain inference
  forbidden_inference an available candidate or a prepared review -> permission to skip native account or execution admission
  binding integrations/mcp/fabric_model.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/native_model.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/fabric_server.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_model.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_model_pipeline.test.mjs

interaction model-commons-records-physical-usage
  source model-commons
  destination financial-metabolism
  relation exact-native-physical-attempt-recording
  preserves the original account key, attempt, realization, occurrence time, receipt digest, measured bytes, duration and admitted rate; exact replay returns one retained event
  drops invented costs, token estimates, zero-price assumptions and inference replay as a response to a lost meter acknowledgement
  forbidden_inference recorded or priced model usage -> an invoice, payment or settled liability
  binding integrations/mcp/native_meter.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/fabric_model.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/native_meter.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/fabric_model_pipeline.test.mjs

interaction account-work-names-provider-sessions-for-meter
  source cmd-meter
  destination aurekai-activity
  relation exact-session-key-read
  preserves the account Work index as owner of task, run and account scope; Meter reads its provider_session_ref read-only and attributes model token receipts only where one task and one provider name the session for the same account key
  drops time-window, title and proximity joins, sessions claimed by more than one task, and evidence recorded under another account key
  forbidden_inference a task's provider session with token evidence -> a cost the account was charged for that task, or a CostAllocation
  binding cmd/BonfyreQueue/src/account_work.h
  binding cmd/BonfyreMeter/src/meter_tokens.h
  witness cmd/BonfyreQueue/tests/account_work_index_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreMeter/tests/token_evidence_test.sh
